From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc64: list the sabre's 64-bit memory space in its ranges,
 as OBP does

The sabre's "ranges" had three entries: configuration, I/O and 32-bit
memory space. OBP on the Ultra 5/10 lists the 64-bit memory space as
well, over the same window, and the pci (psycho/sabre) driver of
Solaris 2.6 refuses a ranges property with fewer than four entries: its
attach fails without a message, nothing below the host bridge attaches,
and the CD boot stops with "Cannot assemble drivers for root
/pci@1f,0/pci@1,1/ide@3/cdrom@2,0:b". Solaris 7 and later, Linux and the
BSDs take the bridge with either list.

Add the fourth entry, 64-bit memory space over the 32-bit window.
---
 arch/sparc64/openbios.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc64/openbios.c b/arch/sparc64/openbios.c
index cba23dc..63b8e62 100644
--- a/arch/sparc64/openbios.c
+++ b/arch/sparc64/openbios.c
@@ -69,7 +69,9 @@ static const struct hwdef hwdefs[] = {
                 { .type = CONFIGURATION_SPACE, .parentaddr = 0, .childaddr = APB_SPECIAL_BASE + 0x1000000ULL, .len = 0x1000000 },
                 { .type = IO_SPACE, .parentaddr = 0, .childaddr = APB_SPECIAL_BASE + 0x2000000ULL, .len = 0x1000000 },
                 { .type = MEMORY_SPACE_32, .parentaddr = 0, .childaddr = APB_MEM_BASE, .len = 0xf0000000 },
-                { .type = 0, .parentaddr = 0, .childaddr = 0, .len = 0 }
+                /* OBP lists the 64-bit memory space as well, over the same
+                   window: Solaris 2.6's pci driver refuses fewer than four */
+                { .type = MEMORY_SPACE_64, .parentaddr = 0, .childaddr = APB_MEM_BASE, .len = 0xf0000000 }
             },
             .irqs = { 0, 1, 2, 3 },
         },
